WEBVTT

00:05.588 --> 00:08.299
<i>Is this really...</i>

00:08.383 --> 00:09.634
Takopi!

00:13.179 --> 00:14.931
Thank you, Takopi,

00:16.182 --> 00:17.726
for killing her for me.

00:19.185 --> 00:21.104
<i>"Taking someone's life."</i>

00:22.022 --> 00:24.399
<i>In your language,</i>

00:24.482 --> 00:26.526
<i>I think it's called "killing."</i>

00:27.694 --> 00:31.364
<i>Shizuka smiled at me.</i>

00:32.866 --> 00:35.118
Let's go, then.

00:36.953 --> 00:41.332
<i>On the third planet
in the solar system, "Earth,"</i>

00:41.916 --> 00:44.544
<i>it's been seven days
since I landed here from Happy Planet.</i>

00:46.713 --> 00:48.173
<i>I can't start over.</i>

00:48.798 --> 00:51.968
<i>My real story</i>

00:53.011 --> 00:54.971
<i>starts from this moment-pi.</i>

01:09.736 --> 01:13.114
TAKOPI'S ORIGINAL SIN

02:06.126 --> 02:10.255
EPISODE 3: TAKOPI'S CONFESSION

02:14.926 --> 02:17.262
I was worried about you,
so I came along to take a look.

02:17.345 --> 02:18.179
Azuma.

02:18.263 --> 02:20.056
What? That's...

02:20.140 --> 02:22.225
Huh? That's creepy!

02:22.934 --> 02:23.893
Azuma.

02:25.228 --> 02:27.105
It spoke?

02:41.536 --> 02:44.747
Marina died because of Takopi's magic.

02:44.831 --> 02:45.707
Pi!

02:45.790 --> 02:48.543
Shizuka, it's not magic.
It's a Happy Gadget.

02:50.086 --> 02:52.881
Takopi is from Happy Planet.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.549
I'm a Happian-pi.

02:55.300 --> 02:57.969
Well... what's it called?

02:58.469 --> 03:00.763
Happy Fruit is delicious, right?

03:00.847 --> 03:01.681
Pi.

03:03.683 --> 03:04.809
No.

03:05.560 --> 03:07.187
This is messed up.

03:09.939 --> 03:11.441
- What is?
- Pi?

03:12.025 --> 03:13.735
And you're still asking me
what's messed up?

03:13.818 --> 03:15.695
I don't get it.

03:16.362 --> 03:18.281
Why did you kill her?

03:18.364 --> 03:19.824
There must've been another way.

03:20.491 --> 03:21.409
But Marina--

03:21.492 --> 03:24.329
And why are you leaving her
and heading back like it's no big deal?

03:24.412 --> 03:26.456
You know it's going
to cause a problem, right?

03:30.210 --> 03:33.087
Azuma, you feel kind of scary-pi.

03:33.171 --> 03:34.631
You should be happier...

03:34.714 --> 03:35.840
You...

03:35.924 --> 03:37.717
Someone died.

03:37.800 --> 03:39.302
What's with that tone?

03:39.385 --> 03:40.637
Are you kidding me?

03:42.472 --> 03:44.390
- I'm sorry.
- Shut up for now.

03:46.684 --> 03:48.061
Azuma.

03:48.686 --> 03:51.689
But Marina died because of magic.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.441
It can't be helped.

03:53.524 --> 03:55.318
Magic can't possibly...

03:57.153 --> 04:00.823
Magic or not, murder is still murder.

04:01.783 --> 04:05.119
I think you'll be sent
to a juvenile detention center.

04:08.831 --> 04:12.543
"An alien killed her"?
That excuse just won't work.

04:15.505 --> 04:18.549
Then I can't see Chappy.

04:18.633 --> 04:20.051
I read it in a book.

04:20.134 --> 04:22.595
If you want to reduce your sentence,
you have to turn yourself in.

04:22.679 --> 04:24.222
Let's go to the police station now.

04:24.931 --> 04:28.518
Azuma, is there another way?

04:29.227 --> 04:30.645
Another way?

04:30.728 --> 04:32.605
Other than turning myself in.

04:32.689 --> 04:35.024
I don't understand the book
you're talking about,

04:35.817 --> 04:37.568
but you seem to know a lot about it.

04:39.112 --> 04:43.199
In novels, they frame someone else.

04:44.200 --> 04:46.286
No, that's fiction.

04:46.369 --> 04:49.247
It's more common to cover up the crime.

04:49.330 --> 04:51.082
That's their usual trick.

04:51.165 --> 04:52.125
I see.

04:53.501 --> 04:55.628
Then let's do it.

04:59.757 --> 05:02.593
Because I don't want
to go to juvenile detention.

05:03.803 --> 05:05.513
Let's do that.

05:06.222 --> 05:09.142
Well, what should we do?

05:09.225 --> 05:10.059
What?

05:10.143 --> 05:12.145
No, that's a crime too.

05:12.812 --> 05:15.023
Besides, kids can't cover it up.

05:15.106 --> 05:17.066
We still have Takopi's magic.

05:18.526 --> 05:19.527
So...

05:20.153 --> 05:23.031
can you help me think of a good way?

05:23.781 --> 05:24.866
There's no way I can...

05:24.949 --> 05:26.117
<i>Hey.</i>

05:26.951 --> 05:28.619
<i>Why can't you do it?</i>

05:30.413 --> 05:34.125
If it's just the two of us,
we'll get caught in no time.

05:34.208 --> 05:37.337
That's why I want you to help me.

05:38.046 --> 05:42.091
I have no friends,
and I can't rely on Mama.

05:43.259 --> 05:45.386
There's no one else I can turn to.

05:47.096 --> 05:48.306
Azuma.

05:48.931 --> 05:51.100
Your brother can do it.

05:51.184 --> 05:52.143
Please.

05:55.438 --> 05:57.523
You're all I have.

05:58.232 --> 05:59.442
Help me.

06:03.321 --> 06:05.573
If it's me, I can do it.

06:07.950 --> 06:10.703
What's a juvenile detention center-pi?

06:10.787 --> 06:11.954
Hey, octopus.

06:19.504 --> 06:20.421
What's this?

06:21.297 --> 06:23.549
That's Memory Box.

06:23.633 --> 06:25.134
I'm not asking about the name.

06:26.010 --> 06:27.470
Let's see.

06:28.054 --> 06:32.266
It preserves whatever you put inside
exactly as it is.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.768
Like pretty leaves.

06:34.602 --> 06:36.521
You can change the size?

06:49.158 --> 06:52.286
For now, let's bury Kirarazaka with this

06:52.370 --> 06:54.664
and hide the murder weapon
inside that octopus.

06:55.164 --> 06:56.249
Pi.

06:56.332 --> 06:57.333
And then...

06:58.709 --> 07:00.670
Pi...

07:00.753 --> 07:02.547
Is this really going to be okay?

07:02.630 --> 07:03.464
Pi.

07:03.548 --> 07:06.884
The Transformation Palette's
transformation is perfect-pi.

07:08.136 --> 07:10.680
- More importantly--
- I'll go get a shovel.

07:11.889 --> 07:14.308
Don't let her family members suspect you.

07:14.392 --> 07:15.893
Otherwise, it'll all be for nothing.

07:18.062 --> 07:19.188
Well...

07:21.232 --> 07:22.525
Um...

07:25.236 --> 07:27.655
Are you really okay with this-pi?

07:28.906 --> 07:29.907
How should I put it?

07:29.991 --> 07:33.035
Like me living on as Marina from now on,

07:33.870 --> 07:35.830
hiding Marina and all that.

07:35.913 --> 07:37.457
All of this...

07:38.040 --> 07:39.667
- Are you really--
- Takopi.

07:41.002 --> 07:43.546
You'll get caught if you talk like that.

07:48.050 --> 07:49.719
I'll do my best-pi!

07:49.802 --> 07:51.596
You said it again.

08:24.921 --> 08:26.589
NO TRESPASSING

08:29.926 --> 08:31.552
<i>As long as I can make Shizuka smile,</i>

08:31.636 --> 08:32.678
KIRARAZAKA'S HOUSE

08:32.762 --> 08:36.307
<i>...I'll do my best to live
as Marina from now on-pi.</i>

08:38.100 --> 08:40.186
<i>I'll be as energetic as Marina.</i>

08:40.770 --> 08:42.480
<i>I'll do my best to be her-pi.</i>

08:56.577 --> 08:58.829
- I'm...
- What the hell are tassels?!

08:58.913 --> 09:02.166
Curtains... the things you put on curtains.

09:04.794 --> 09:07.588
How dare you use my money
to do something so ridiculous?

09:07.672 --> 09:08.673
You parasite!

09:08.756 --> 09:09.674
I'm...

09:09.757 --> 09:11.884
You're at the hostess bar day and night,
and you have the nerve to say that?

09:11.968 --> 09:12.802
I can

09:12.885 --> 09:14.679
spend my hard-earned money

09:14.762 --> 09:17.139
on whatever I want!

09:17.223 --> 09:18.266
I'm... home.

09:25.231 --> 09:28.526
What would you have done
if it got in her eye?

09:28.609 --> 09:31.112
She's a girl.
If she gets a scar on her face...

09:31.195 --> 09:35.408
It's not like she's hurt.
Marina also said she's fine.

09:35.491 --> 09:40.121
Mari could even ask you for compensation.

09:40.204 --> 09:42.623
You're always so paranoid.

09:42.707 --> 09:44.083
That's not constructive at all.

09:44.792 --> 09:47.461
This is why I can't stand a bitch
who's never worked a day in her life.

09:47.545 --> 09:49.714
- You're so mean. For you and Mari,
- <i>Marina's papa and mama</i>

09:49.797 --> 09:51.882
- I've been giving my all to this family.
- <i>talk a lot every day.</i>

09:51.966 --> 09:54.802
- <i>They really get along well-pi.</i>
- You love taking all the credit.

09:54.885 --> 09:57.096
You think crying solves everything.

09:57.722 --> 10:00.099
Let's go see Chappy, then.

10:00.808 --> 10:02.435
Sounds good-pi.

10:02.518 --> 10:03.936
No, no, no.

10:04.020 --> 10:06.022
I told you, we can't go right now.

10:06.606 --> 10:09.775
Chappy's with your dad in Tokyo, right?

10:09.859 --> 10:11.986
It'll be too hard for kids like us
to go there on our own.

10:12.570 --> 10:13.988
Besides,

10:14.071 --> 10:17.074
- let's wait until this octopus settles in.
- Pi...

10:17.158 --> 10:21.245
By the way, what's a divorce mediation-pi?

10:21.329 --> 10:23.581
That's what Marina's mama said-pi.

10:24.540 --> 10:26.792
The other one's already buried,
so it should be fine.

10:26.876 --> 10:28.753
But we shouldn't leave town for a while.

10:30.046 --> 10:32.131
If we start planning carefully now,

10:32.214 --> 10:33.466
TOP SECRET: SUMMER BREAK PLANNER
CLASS 4-1, NAOKI AZUMA

10:34.091 --> 10:36.135
...we'll carry it out during summer break.

10:36.218 --> 10:38.763
Until then, we'll have a strategy meeting
every day after school.

10:39.513 --> 10:40.723
Got it?

10:42.224 --> 10:43.517
I got it.

10:43.601 --> 10:44.602
Good.

10:49.857 --> 10:52.860
<i>No, I don't have time for this.</i>

10:52.943 --> 10:54.987
<i>I have to go home quickly and study today.</i>

10:55.071 --> 10:56.280
Hey.

10:57.114 --> 10:59.283
- It's quite rare for you to play outside.
- <i>Pi?</i>

11:00.117 --> 11:01.661
Are these your classmates?

11:02.328 --> 11:03.663
Junya...

11:03.746 --> 11:06.749
So you've completely stopped
calling me your brother, huh?

11:06.832 --> 11:09.418
Are you Azuma's big brother-pi?

11:09.502 --> 11:11.170
Pi?

11:11.253 --> 11:13.255
That's right.

11:13.339 --> 11:15.841
You're home early too.

11:15.925 --> 11:19.053
Nah, I'm heading to my part-time job now.

11:19.637 --> 11:22.431
Can you calm Mom down for me?

11:23.683 --> 11:24.892
Sure.

11:25.726 --> 11:27.103
Pi.

11:28.145 --> 11:29.313
Junya...

11:29.397 --> 11:32.316
He doesn't need a part-time job at all.

11:32.942 --> 11:35.528
He can get as much allowance as he wants.

11:36.195 --> 11:38.114
But he always makes Mom worry like that.

11:38.197 --> 11:39.573
Is that so-pi?

11:39.657 --> 11:43.494
He even used his own money
to buy that stupid freaking ring.

11:44.078 --> 11:46.497
All he needs to do is study.

11:47.540 --> 11:50.918
Everyone expects the most from him,
more than anyone else.

11:52.670 --> 11:54.046
Azuma.

11:54.880 --> 11:56.966
- Kuze...
- Just take it away.

11:59.343 --> 12:00.553
The ring.

12:00.636 --> 12:04.432
If that happens, he'll quit
his part-time job after falling apart.

12:06.392 --> 12:08.519
No, I don't think he'll do that.

12:09.270 --> 12:10.604
Besides, it's theft.

12:10.688 --> 12:12.064
How should I put it?

12:13.733 --> 12:16.110
I think you can do it.

12:20.614 --> 12:22.283
AZUMA CLINIC

12:25.786 --> 12:28.038
Is this Azuma's house-pi?

12:29.123 --> 12:30.750
So what should we take-pi?

12:30.833 --> 12:32.418
You... Shut up.

12:32.501 --> 12:35.838
If anything happens,
there's still Takopi's magic.

12:35.921 --> 12:37.256
Pi.

12:37.339 --> 12:38.174
That's true,

12:38.257 --> 12:41.343
- I'm so happy-pi, Azuma.
- <i>but I have to take him home with me.</i>

12:41.427 --> 12:42.261
Pi!

12:44.680 --> 12:45.639
<i>All right.</i>

12:45.723 --> 12:48.017
<i>Junya only takes off his ring
when he takes a bath.</i>

12:49.143 --> 12:50.936
<i>It should be in his room now.</i>

12:55.900 --> 12:56.817
<i>There it is.</i>

12:57.860 --> 12:59.403
That's great-pi.

13:00.321 --> 13:01.864
Okay, I just need to take this.

13:01.947 --> 13:03.324
<i>Look at this.</i>

13:04.492 --> 13:06.035
I finally bought it.

13:06.118 --> 13:07.995
It matches the one my girlfriend has.

13:08.621 --> 13:12.249
You really have to buy things like this
with your own money.

13:13.375 --> 13:15.669
<i>Why is he pretending to be all normal?</i>

13:16.712 --> 13:21.342
<i>When he can get anything he wants.</i>

13:22.134 --> 13:25.805
By the way, you've been using that
for a long time, right?

13:26.514 --> 13:28.682
Next time when I get paid,

13:28.766 --> 13:29.642
I'll help you get...

13:37.566 --> 13:39.652
Will you get in trouble
if he finds out-pi?

13:39.735 --> 13:41.862
Hey, can't you do something
with your gadgets?

13:42.446 --> 13:44.281
I don't know-pi.

13:44.365 --> 13:46.867
It's not that-pi, or this-pi.

13:47.618 --> 13:48.619
Oh, no.

13:51.747 --> 13:53.958
My phone...

14:01.924 --> 14:03.676
Did I open the window?

14:08.889 --> 14:09.974
This is bad.

14:10.057 --> 14:11.100
We'll be in trouble if he sees us.

14:11.183 --> 14:12.268
Let's run, octopus!

14:12.351 --> 14:15.396
Pi. Azuma, this way-pi.

14:15.980 --> 14:16.939
I know...

14:20.651 --> 14:23.112
<i>Weight limit exceeded.</i>

14:23.696 --> 14:26.198
<i>- Battery depleted.
- No way.</i>

14:31.996 --> 14:33.038
That's odd.

14:33.914 --> 14:35.583
I thought I heard something.

14:36.792 --> 14:38.252
Am I imagining things?

14:39.336 --> 14:41.338
Pi...

14:44.967 --> 14:45.801
I'm saved...

14:45.885 --> 14:47.344
<i>Weight limit exceeded.</i>

14:47.428 --> 14:48.262
I'm not!

14:48.345 --> 14:49.930
Pi!

14:54.518 --> 14:57.271
Pi...

15:00.024 --> 15:01.358
Azuma.

15:02.234 --> 15:03.986
Are you okay-pi?

15:12.620 --> 15:14.788
Are you hurt anywhere-pi?

15:16.832 --> 15:18.250
I see-pi.

15:20.669 --> 15:22.630
I'm glad, pi.

15:27.927 --> 15:28.886
But

15:29.511 --> 15:32.264
we didn't get the ring-pi.

15:33.349 --> 15:35.142
- I can't do--
- <i>Too bad.</i>

15:36.268 --> 15:38.312
Then as punishment,

15:38.395 --> 15:40.731
I'll confiscate your pancakes.

15:42.608 --> 15:45.152
Your brother always gets full marks.

15:46.236 --> 15:47.488
You can bear with it, right?

15:47.571 --> 15:48.989
Mama!

15:50.199 --> 15:51.575
Then next time...

15:53.535 --> 15:55.788
Next time, I'll definitely score...

15:57.456 --> 15:59.792
You didn't get to eat it again.

15:59.875 --> 16:02.628
I went to all that trouble to make it.

16:02.711 --> 16:05.297
I'm sorry. I'll endure it today.

16:05.381 --> 16:06.674
I'll do better next time.

16:06.757 --> 16:08.008
Somehow,

16:08.842 --> 16:11.095
I feel like I'm wasting my time here.

16:12.388 --> 16:15.516
No matter what I do, you're still...

16:15.599 --> 16:16.558
<i>Wait.</i>

16:19.687 --> 16:20.980
<i>Wait.</i>

16:23.148 --> 16:24.441
<i>Please don't...</i>

16:25.484 --> 16:27.027
<i>give up on me.</i>

16:36.620 --> 16:37.997
What's wrong, you two?

16:38.080 --> 16:39.498
You look pathetic.

16:40.249 --> 16:41.792
Pathetic-pi?

17:18.328 --> 17:19.538
A DEEP DIVE INTO TOKYO

17:31.008 --> 17:33.552
SHIZUKA - CHAPPY

17:33.635 --> 17:34.511
THINGS TO PREPARE FOOD - LUNCHBOX

17:34.595 --> 17:35.512
ACCOMMODATION - INN? MONEY - ALLOWANCE

18:17.638 --> 18:22.684
I found out something terrible
at your place the other day-pi.

18:23.477 --> 18:27.314
Humans will exceed the weight limit
when they wear Flappy Flappy Wings.

18:27.397 --> 18:31.235
We can't fly to Tokyo, where Chappy is-pi.

18:31.902 --> 18:35.739
It doesn't matter.
I wasn't looking forward to it anyway.

18:35.823 --> 18:37.074
Is that so-pi?

18:37.574 --> 18:39.576
Then we'll have to go by ship
or bullet train.

18:39.660 --> 18:40.494
Pi.

18:40.577 --> 18:42.371
The only problem now is the money.

18:42.454 --> 18:43.705
Pi.

18:43.789 --> 18:44.790
MEANS OF TRANSPORTATION

18:44.873 --> 18:45.999
Hey.

18:46.083 --> 18:48.710
Why are Happy Gadgets so useless?

18:48.794 --> 18:50.129
Pi?

18:50.212 --> 18:52.756
How could you even come
to Earth like that?

18:52.840 --> 18:54.800
That's not true-pi.

18:54.883 --> 18:58.846
Happy Planet has other happier gadgets-pi.

18:58.929 --> 19:00.597
Like the Saturn Dog Diorama.

19:00.681 --> 19:01.765
That's trash.

19:02.933 --> 19:05.144
There's also the Happy Big Clock.

19:05.227 --> 19:08.814
It's a great gadget that lets you travel
through time anytime, anywhere.

19:08.897 --> 19:10.816
Then bring it here right now!

19:10.899 --> 19:13.152
We can then pretend
that none of this happened, right?

19:13.819 --> 19:15.529
Pi... I can't do that-pi.

19:15.612 --> 19:16.530
Darn it.

19:16.613 --> 19:19.575
Because I can't go back
to Happy Planet-pi.

19:19.658 --> 19:20.868
Hey.

19:21.493 --> 19:22.536
Kuze.

19:22.619 --> 19:25.164
I'm thinking of taking
the bullet train to Tokyo.

19:26.665 --> 19:28.167
Let's play, then.

19:31.295 --> 19:34.381
<i>It's fun when the three
of us are together-pi.</i>

19:35.174 --> 19:37.134
<i>Shizuka smiles too.</i>

19:37.217 --> 19:39.803
<i>I wish we could live like this forever.</i>

19:42.139 --> 19:43.348
<i>Huh?</i>

19:43.432 --> 19:48.353
<i>By the way,
why can't I go back to Happy Planet-pi?</i>

19:49.479 --> 19:52.274
- In the end, you didn't even show up
- <i>Hmm, I have</i>

19:52.357 --> 19:53.984
- to Mom's 60th birthday party.
- <i>no idea-pi.</i>

19:54.067 --> 19:57.321
I have plans too.

19:57.404 --> 19:59.531
It's just some homemaker class
that doesn't make any money!

19:59.615 --> 20:03.076
You're the one who never comes home
from the hostess bar.

20:03.160 --> 20:05.871
What's wrong with drinking
with the money I earned?

20:06.747 --> 20:10.125
How could you be so cold to my parents?

20:11.043 --> 20:12.336
Right, Marina?

20:13.545 --> 20:15.047
What is it-pi?

20:15.130 --> 20:17.716
Mari, you're talking like that again.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.135
Is it a trend at school?

20:20.219 --> 20:22.971
Marina, you've become more
cheerful lately. It's nice.

20:23.513 --> 20:25.766
Mama, on the other hand,
is still as annoying.

20:28.435 --> 20:31.563
Marina, do you want
to come to Papa's place?

20:32.189 --> 20:34.358
- We've settled on custody, haven't we?
- <i>Papa's place?</i>

20:34.441 --> 20:35.859
You don't even want to raise her.

20:35.943 --> 20:36.777
What?

20:36.860 --> 20:40.447
<i>Does he mean Tokyo, where Chappy is?</i>

20:42.699 --> 20:45.244
I want to go-pi to Papa's place!

20:45.327 --> 20:47.204
Oh, I see.

20:47.287 --> 20:50.832
Then Marina, come to Papa's place.

20:50.916 --> 20:52.292
Pi.

20:52.376 --> 20:54.920
I see. You're coming?

20:55.003 --> 20:56.338
<i>Yay!</i>

21:01.885 --> 21:02.761
<i>Mari.</i>

21:03.762 --> 21:05.430
Papa said he's not coming home today.

21:06.014 --> 21:07.015
Pi.

21:07.099 --> 21:10.102
- <i>Yay-pi. I have to tell Azuma.</i>
- What's with that way of talking?

21:10.185 --> 21:12.187
<i>I might be able to go
before summer break-pi.</i>

21:12.271 --> 21:13.188
Hey.

21:13.272 --> 21:14.231
<i>Yay-pi.</i>

21:14.314 --> 21:16.483
<i>If that's the case,
I'm sure Shizuka will be happy too.</i>

21:16.566 --> 21:17.693
Mari.

21:19.069 --> 21:20.570
What's the matter-pi, Mama?

21:20.654 --> 21:21.571
The way you talk.

21:21.655 --> 21:23.490
Oh, right-pi.

21:24.574 --> 21:25.951
<i>I have to be careful-pi.</i>

21:26.034 --> 21:28.662
<i>Because from now on,
I'll be living as Marina...</i>

21:34.376 --> 21:36.586
The way you talk is too vulgar.

21:37.212 --> 21:38.297
Can you fix it?

21:41.383 --> 21:42.718
Sorry-pi.

21:45.595 --> 21:47.514
- Mama...
- Mari.

21:49.641 --> 21:50.475
Mari.

21:51.351 --> 21:53.312
You understand, don't you? Mari.

21:54.521 --> 21:55.605
Mari.

21:55.689 --> 21:57.691
I won't do it again.

21:57.774 --> 21:59.109
Mari, you've really changed.

21:59.901 --> 22:02.487
You always used to be on my side.

22:02.571 --> 22:04.656
You were a good girl and listened to me.

22:04.740 --> 22:07.117
The past? Then I'll change.

22:07.200 --> 22:08.410
I'll go back to the way I was.

22:08.493 --> 22:11.830
No...

22:11.913 --> 22:13.582
Everything is wrong!

22:13.665 --> 22:15.834
- Even if that person couldn't tell
- Mama is scary.

22:15.917 --> 22:17.419
- or didn't notice!
- Mama.

22:17.502 --> 22:19.004
But I know.

22:19.087 --> 22:21.298
Mari isn't like this!

22:21.381 --> 22:22.924
Someone like you...

22:23.008 --> 22:24.384
Stop!

22:41.568 --> 22:42.736
Please,

22:44.363 --> 22:46.323
give Marina back to me.

22:48.700 --> 22:50.535
I don't know who you are.

22:52.204 --> 22:56.500
But I carried Marina for ten months
and gave birth to her.

22:56.583 --> 22:58.710
She's my precious daughter.

23:00.587 --> 23:02.631
Mari, I'm sorry.

23:02.714 --> 23:04.674
I haven't been a good mother, have I?

23:05.175 --> 23:08.762
But I really love you, so please.

23:10.472 --> 23:11.932
Come back.

23:17.687 --> 23:21.274
<i>Marina did terrible things to Shizuka.</i>

23:22.025 --> 23:23.026
<i>But...</i>

23:54.391 --> 23:55.684
Marina,

23:56.685 --> 23:58.186
I'm sorry.

23:59.062 --> 24:01.440
Marina's papa and mama,

24:02.190 --> 24:04.860
I'm sorry that I'm not Marina.

24:05.694 --> 24:08.780
I'm sorry that I can't
reunite you with her.

24:12.284 --> 24:13.994
Marina.

24:16.121 --> 24:20.041
I'm sorry that I killed you.

24:24.963 --> 24:26.381
<i>I need to think.</i>

24:27.799 --> 24:31.511
<i>What have I done? How can I undo this?</i>

24:32.095 --> 24:33.305
<i>Takopi.</i>

24:34.139 --> 24:36.308
<i>And what should I do next?</i>

24:36.391 --> 24:37.684
<i>Takopi.</i>

24:43.148 --> 24:45.108
Thank you, Takopi,

24:45.942 --> 24:47.819
for killing her for me.

24:52.866 --> 24:53.742
<i>And...</i>

24:54.910 --> 24:58.747
<i>I need to talk to Shizuka again.</i>

25:03.001 --> 25:04.336
GEOLOGICAL SURVEY IN PROGRESS

25:04.419 --> 25:05.420
NO TRESPASSING

25:06.004 --> 25:08.048
Hey, there's something here!

25:08.131 --> 25:10.050
Hey, what is this?

25:10.842 --> 25:11.843
What is it?

25:12.594 --> 25:14.930
This doesn't look good.

25:16.598 --> 25:17.849
A kid?
